QtWebEngine's distribution ships content/public/test/ with only android/ and
test_service.mojom in it, so three headers the vendored Content Shell utility
client includes are simply absent:

    ../../content/shell/utility/shell_content_utility_client.h:9:10: fatal
    error: content/public/test/audio_service_test_helper.h: No such file or
    directory

(network_service_test_helper.h and test_service.h are missing the same way;
the compile stops at the first one.) test_service.mojom.h is unaffected --
it is generated from test_service.mojom, which is present.

Everything these three headers provide is browser-test scaffolding, not
functionality this port's content_shell needs:

- NetworkServiceTestHelper and AudioServiceTestHelper are constructed only
  inside `if (is_browsertest && ...)`, and is_browsertest is set only when
  shell_content_main.cc sees the browser-test switch.
- TestService is instantiated only for the kTestServiceUrl service name.

So this follows U0001's precedent of compiling out test-only Shell hooks on
this port rather than vendoring the missing sources: guard the includes, the
two member pointers, their construction, the TestService branch, and the one
RegisterNetworkBinders call that dereferences the network helper, all behind
!defined(OS_HAIKU).

Vendoring the three headers instead was considered and rejected: their
implementations pull in more of content/public/test (and its GN targets),
which the distribution also drops, to support a mode this build never runs.

